Scope of change
---------------
- New module tests/acceptance/week4/seed-nguyen.mjs exporting seedNguyen(ctx)
  and contextFromProject(project) + a --project CLI. It does not modify
  tests/acceptance/seed.mjs or week2/seed.mjs: wiring the call into Huu's seed
  needs Huu's agreement (plan N20), so the exact line is documented instead.
- New pure helper module tests/acceptance/week4/seed-lib.mjs:
  5 deterministic KYC slots, drift gate, idempotency planners, BigInt drift
  classifier and the synthetic PNG generator.
- New tests tests/acceptance/week4/seed-nguyen.test.mjs (node --test).
- tests/acceptance/README.md: new "Tuan 4 / N20" section with command, flag,
  ordering (RC1 before, A8 after), idempotency and evidence paths.

What the seed creates on a running acceptance stack
---------------------------------------------------
1) 5 pending KYC profiles (week4.kyc01..05@demo.vn):
   - signup through POST /api/auth/signup (real Gateway path);
   - front and back uploaded ONCE through POST /api/users/kyc/documents,
     expected 202, PNG/JPEG <= 5 MB;
   - images are synthetic 900x560 PNG built from an SVG that says
     "SYNTHETIC IMAGE - NOT AN ID DOCUMENT" (no real person, no real ID);
   - deterministic idNumber per slot (000000000401..405);
   - no direct DB insert and no review/approval, so they stay PENDING.
2) 5 sample notifications, type WALLET_CREDITED, created through the internal
   route POST /api/notifications of notification-service with x-internal-key
   read from /run/secrets/internal_key inside the container (the port is not
   published to the host). Deterministic eventId
   week4-seed-<slot>-wallet-credited -> Inbox dedupe on rerun. Message contains
   only the demo credit amount, no secrets.
   Each account receives a REAL 50.000 VND ledger credit with a fixed
   referenceId (week4-kyc-<slot>-credit), so the notification is truthful and
   the credit replays instead of duplicating.
3) Exactly 1 deliberate drift wallet (week4.drift@demo.vn):
   - real 200.000 VND ledger credit (referenceId week4-drift-credit);
   - then UPDATE "Wallet".balance += 5000 for that wallet id only;
   - no ledger entry is updated or deleted, no other wallet is touched.
   - The wallet id is printed and stored in week4-seed.json for A8.

Guard rails
-----------
- assertDriftAllowed refuses NODE_ENV=production and refuses any run without
  SEED_ALLOW_DRIFT=1, before the drift account is created. Unit-tested.
- The drift wallet is the dedicated week4.drift@demo.vn account, asserted not
  to be an/binh/chi/highlands/admin nor a SYSTEM wallet.
- Conservation: SUM(balance) over every wallet EXCEPT the drift wallet must be
  0 and is asserted after the run (all credits move money from a SYSTEM wallet,
  so ledger-backed balances net to zero). The drift wallet differs from its
  ledger by exactly 5.000 VND.
- Nothing is written to production data: the module only runs inside a
  finvault-acceptance-<12 hex> project.

Idempotency (run twice -> no duplicates)
----------------------------------------
- Accounts: found by fixed email in auth_service; existing email -> no signup.
- KYC: upload only when the profile row is absent or kyc_status = NONE; PENDING,
  APPROVED and REJECTED are preserved (a rerun never resets a review).
- Credits: deterministic referenceId; the ledger replays the same operation.
- Notifications: deterministic eventId; the notification Inbox returns
  duplicate=true instead of inserting a second row.
- Drift: classifyDrift compares wallet.balance with the signed ledger sum using
  BigInt: equal -> apply, +5000 -> skip, anything else -> throw.

Commands and actual results
---------------------------
1) node --check tests/acceptance/week4/seed-nguyen.mjs
   node --check tests/acceptance/week4/seed-lib.mjs
   PASS - both exited 0 (ESM syntax valid).

2) node --test tests/acceptance/week4/seed-nguyen.test.mjs
   PASS - tests 8, pass 8, fail 0, skipped 0, duration ~0.25-1.6s.
   Test names:
   - seed module exports the Week-4 entry points (5 unique KYC slots, reserved
     demo emails excluded);
   - synthetic documents are PNG, 900x560, under 5 MB and side-specific
     (verified with sharp metadata; front != back);
   - drift gate refuses production and any run without the explicit flag
     (4 rejection/allow cases);
   - idempotency planner creates only missing slots and converges to empty
     (all, partial with mixed case, full rerun);
   - KYC upload happens once: only NONE/absent state is uploadable;
   - drift classifier applies once, skips on rerun and rejects unknown states
     (including "200000.00" decimals);
   - notification event ids are deterministic and unique per slot;
   - contextFromProject rejects malformed or unknown projects without Docker.
   No Docker, PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ or Gateway is needed for these tests.

3) npm run check (Backend root)
   NOT_APPLICABLE - there is no root package.json in PTPMHDV_Backend; each
   service owns its own scripts. This change only adds .mjs acceptance files
   and README text, so no service typecheck/build is affected.

Summary
-------
PASS: node --check (2 files), node --test 8/8.
FAIL: none.
SKIP: none.
NOT_RUN: real seed execution against a live acceptance stack (Compose,
      PostgreSQL, MinIO, RabbitMQ, notification-service) and therefore also:
      - five PENDING KYC rows visible in Admin after the seed;
      - five notifications visible in the N15 notification UI;
      - RC1 isBalanced=true before the drift, and the A8 drift anomaly after it.
      Reason: this machine has no Docker/PostgreSQL/RabbitMQ and no acceptance
      project. Nothing above is claimed as PASS.

Open items / hand-off
---------------------
- H15 coordination: tests/acceptance/seed.mjs (Huu's file) is intentionally NOT
  modified. To run the Week-4 seed as part of the shared command, Huu must agree
  to add:
    import { seedNguyen } from './week4/seed-nguyen.mjs'
    // inside seed(ctx): await seedNguyen(ctx)
  Until then the module runs via
    $env:SEED_ALLOW_DRIFT = '1'
    node tests/acceptance/week4/seed-nguyen.mjs --project finvault-acceptance-<id>
  after the base seed created accounts.json.
- SEED_ALLOW_DRIFT must only be set for deliberate A8 runs. Without it the seed
  refuses to create the drift wallet. NODE_ENV=production always refuses.
- Ordering: run RC1 before this seed if isBalanced=true is expected; run A8
  after. The drift makes every later reconciliation report show one
  BALANCE_DRIFT_QUICK/FULL anomaly on that wallet by design.
- Credentials for the five demo accounts are generated randomly and stored in
  .cache/acceptance-week2/<project>/week4-accounts.json (mode 0600, ignored, not
  committed, never logged).
- If a KYC account exists in auth_service but its stored password file is lost
  and its profile is still NONE, the seed stops with an explicit message rather
  than guessing a password.
